WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.603 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:09.576
-Hey, everybody.
I said CDs, compact discs,

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:12.478
was an example of an acronym.
That's initialism.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:16.315
An acronym has to make
a new word, like scuba --

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.652
self-contained underwater
breathing apparatus --

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.287
or jackal --

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.357
jerks attempting comedy-killing
absent love.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.126
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:32.765
Instead of street sweeper,

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:36.102
I said sweet streeper.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:39.939
In my defense, I used to work...

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.141
In high school,
I worked at a video store

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:45.144
and we had a section

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.580
called Sweet Streepers,

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.251
which were just
all her best.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.552
"Africa."

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.221
"Choice."

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:58.224
"Heartburn."

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.893
"Ironweed."

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:04.397
Th-The dingo one.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:08.300
"Kramer vs. Kramer."

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.204
Which...

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.340
Not to bring the room down...

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.777
Sal told me there's a leaked
draft from the Supreme Court

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:23.817
They're overturning
Kramer vs. Kramer.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.621
6-3, the conservatives.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.491
It's now -- they're now
ruling in favor of Kramer.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.226
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:37.496
And it was precedent.

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.899
But they just, they don't care.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.734
Such a great cast.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.670
That movie's great --
"Kramer vs. Kramer."

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.173
Meryl Streep,
Michael Richards.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.309
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.647
[As Kramer] "He's my boy!"

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.182
[Normal voice]
Remember that scene?

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:01.221
It did -- it's a true story.
I did work in a video store.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:05.925
Maloney Video in Bedford,
New Hampshire.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:09.395
And I was thinking
about it today because,

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.231
again, this is early '90s.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:14.100
I worked there with Mr. Maloney,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.936
and sometimes
it would just be me.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:22.041
And there was not an adult film
section in Maloney Video.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:27.480
What there was was a big book
with -- like, a metal book

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.384
that, the way you would have,
like, pictures in a photo album.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.453
But it was just the
flattened-out cardboard cases

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:36.188
of adult films.

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:39.358
And guys would come in
and just like -- fwonk!

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:42.095
And, like, go through it

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:45.097
and then would give
Mr. Maloney a number.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:47.233
And sometimes they'd come in
and Mr. Maloney would be, like,

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.834
in the back throwing out garbage
or something,

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.069
and it would just be me.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.204
And I could always clock
the guys who were like,

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:54.507
"Oh, nah!"

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.475
'Cause they definitely
wanted to look in the book,

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:57.810
but they didn't want to do it

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.313
while like a 14-year-old kid
was there.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.914
So they'd just, like,
wander around for a while

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:04.951
and then just be like, "I guess
I'll just get 'Flashdance.'"

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:08.587
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:12.292
Hey, I talked about the fact
that somebody made...

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:15.794
'Cause we talked about
Wally being "Two Trees."

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:17.163
And somebody made this,
and I said

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:20.466
this was so nice because
we never get fan art.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.001
Somebody said
this isn't fan art.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.169
This is just a meme.
Also, I missed earlier

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:26.405
that Wally in this
is holding a cue card

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:28.074
that says "Seth sucks."

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.642
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.814
And so somebody, though,
said they felt bad

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.550
that they had never --
we've never gotten fan art,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.552
and look what somebody made
for us.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:43.856
There we go.
There's old Two Trees.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.893
I feel like this is not the
kindest fan art for you, Wally.

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:52.865
I said Two Tree Wally and people
really strongly online

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.368
feel like it should be
Wally Two Trees, right?

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:58.437
That's better.
Yeah, Wally Two Trees is better.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:03.442
And then we really do have -- we
have a crew here of good names.

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:07.880
We had Wally Two Trees,
Mikey the Shoe,

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.016
Tank Top Scollins.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.685
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.688
15 to 16 Reillys.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.557
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.629
Ooh.
I had a scare this week.

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:27.367
So, we have a board,
a beautiful board in my office

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.570
with the guests who are coming
up each day as a little box.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:34.340
You can picture it.
And it has a...

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.676
Because I want to stress --
I hope you know

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.278
I never want to meet
any of you in person.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:40.946
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:43.182
And so this is, like,
we had Sandler on this week.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.884
So that's what it looks...
So I look at the board,

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.485
I'm like,
"Oh, great, Adam Sandler's on."

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:49.888
Or I'll look and I'll be like,
"Oh, Kylie Minogue is on."

00:04:49.888 --> 00:04:53.893
And we had Jensen Ackles
on yesterday.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.028
So I walk in, I'm like, "Aah!"

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.830
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.872
[ Chuckles ]
We had a joke about someone --

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:11.177
true story -- smeared cake
on the glass case

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:14.013
that the Mona Lisa
is behind at the Louvre.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:17.149
And our punchline was they also
did it on the Picasso,

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:18.718
but no one could tell.

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:21.386
And a bunch of you pointed out
there wouldn't be a Picasso

00:05:21.386 --> 00:05:22.721
hanging in the Louvre,

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:24.357
because it's not art?

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:31.730
Also, I was told
I'm pronouncing Louvre wrong.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.732
I was surprised.
But again,

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:36.903
let's take advantage of the fact
that my mom is a French teacher.

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.205
Madame Meyers,
how would you say it?

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.706
-Khan!

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:42.675
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.917
-We have subsets of jackals.

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:53.886
I think that the biggest mistake
you can make

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:56.222
is all jackals are the same.

00:05:56.222 --> 00:06:00.826
One is the kind
that wants to add comedy

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:02.494
via their comments -- jokels.

00:06:02.494 --> 00:06:06.866
And every now and then,
one of them comes through.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.334
And I would like
to compliment -- you know,

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:13.606
we were talking about
Werner's Originals,

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:17.142
and then we showed
the Klaus Kinski candies

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:19.645
that were Fitzcaramellos.

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:22.114
And someone said we missed one.
And I was like,

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.283
"Let's show me your best, kid."

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.885
And there you go.

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:27.887
Nosfera-Chews.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.589
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.797 --> 00:06:40.433
I talked about Donna.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:45.571
My dresser extraordinaire.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:48.140
And this one also,
I will say, made me laugh.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.843
Someone said, "You wear
button-ups and a sweater --

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.678
you need a dresser?"

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:55.648
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:59.085
They added, "Do you also have
a changing table?"

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:00.820
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.959
Hey, sometimes it's --
sometimes it's fair.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.764
"A Closer Look" yesterday,
I guess we talked about

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:15.601
how I was in a sexy
fireman calendar.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.370
And of course, we write these

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:21.039
and then leave it
to Graphics to decide.

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:23.108
And, you know,
I made it very clear

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:25.444
they [bleep] me with this.

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:28.914
And then someone else said,
"Yeah, even worse,

00:07:28.914 --> 00:07:32.017
the weeks on calendars
start on Sunday, not Monday."

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:33.819
So this is
a poorly made calendar.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:37.222
Well, and...

00:07:37.222 --> 00:07:39.891
And now I'm...

00:07:39.891 --> 00:07:41.427
Now I'm realizing they did that

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:43.396
so I would show it
a second time.

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.465
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.135
Damn it.

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:54.273
So, again, I think a lot of you
don't believe me.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:55.841
I want to stress it's true.

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:57.676
I read all these comments.

00:07:57.676 --> 00:08:01.314
And I've noticed a new thing
has started happening

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:04.583
where a lot of your comments
have one reply

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:07.420
and the reply is the same.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:12.692
And it has -- for its avatar,
it has our logo.

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:19.531
And it's weirdly -- it's bold
and it's very clearly a bot,

00:08:19.531 --> 00:08:22.535
but it's trying to engage
with you by having our logo.

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.637
And it has --
this is what it says.

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:26.739
on every one,
it's the same every time.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.941
And I guess it's trying
to trick people into thinking

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:30.709
it's me talking to them.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:32.044
"Thanks for watching.

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:33.712
Send a direct message
right away.

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:36.048
I will love to hear
your thoughts on it

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:38.050
and for more enlightenment."

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:41.721
It's in my voice.

00:08:41.721 --> 00:08:43.289
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:50.996
I would be so happy,
nothing would make me happier,

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:54.600
if at least one of you right now
is watching this and realizing,

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.602
[gasps] "It's not him?!"

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:58.704
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:02.974
[ Humming ]

00:09:02.974 --> 00:09:04.543
Oh, we made a joke
about dog years.

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:07.613
You know, seven -- I had always
assumed one human year,

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.648
seven dog years.

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:12.351
I guess there was
a study in 2019.

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.186
The thinking on this
has changed.

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:17.289
It is not 7 to 1. That is...

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:18.657
It's a little reductive.

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:20.392
It is -- this is --
I'm not --

00:09:20.392 --> 00:09:22.795
Again...

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:27.133
I don't care about this enough
to make it up.

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:29.334
It's for a medium-size dog,

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:32.571
it's 15 years
for the first year.

00:09:32.571 --> 00:09:34.006
This is, again...

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:35.975
Year two is about nine years.

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:40.445
And after that, it's five years
for every human year.

00:09:40.445 --> 00:09:43.816
That's what they told me.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:47.786
And then there's a song
to help remember,

00:09:47.786 --> 00:09:49.989
'cause I guess it's a little
more confusing, obviously.

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:52.824
♪ 15 years when they are 1,
when the second year is seven ♪

00:09:52.824 --> 00:09:55.461
♪ After that it's five each year
until they go to heaven ♪

00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:57.797
♪ 15, 7, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5 ♪

00:09:57.797 --> 00:09:59.832
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:03.169
It's even slower
for small dogs.

00:10:03.169 --> 00:10:05.738
So, smaller dogs,
they age even slower,

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:07.974
which means in just a few years,

00:10:07.974 --> 00:10:10.443
Samberg will be older
than Frisbee.

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:11.944
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:15.080
We were talking about dogs

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.515
'cause we were talking
about "Air Bud."

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:20.385
And one of you left a comment,
"I went to high school with

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:24.557
one of the volleyball players
on "Air Bud Spikes Back."

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:27.626
Well, we'd love to get you
on the show to talk about that.

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:29.362
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:36.434
We did...

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:38.404
I talked about somebody
because someone, one of you

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:41.040
thought the first "Air Bud" was
about football, not basketball.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.976
And you corrected me,
and then I...

00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:45.811
well, you know, my happiest is

00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:47.412
when I can tell a jackal
they were wrong.

00:10:47.412 --> 00:10:52.885
And I went so far to say,
"You erred, bud," which is...

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:55.120
If you want to ever see
that written,

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.189
it'll be etched
on my tombstone.

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:02.928
A bunch of you --
I was surprised.

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:04.763
A bunch of you said
I said "erred" wrong.

00:11:04.763 --> 00:11:08.066
Like, to make a mistake
is not to "air," it's "urr."

00:11:08.066 --> 00:11:09.968
"Urred."

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:13.038
According to the Cambridge
English Dictionary

00:11:13.038 --> 00:11:15.908
and the American rapper Nelly.

00:11:15.908 --> 00:11:17.543
[ Laughter ]

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:25.718
That's the most just for
Shoemaker joke I've ever done.

00:11:27.886 --> 00:11:30.022
And I called him up.
I called up Nelly and he said,

00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:32.691
"Yeah, hurr we say urr."
And I said, "Are you share?"

00:11:32.691 --> 00:11:34.527
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:42.567
We talked about the fact...

00:11:42.567 --> 00:11:45.971
So, Lauren Boebert
called out politicians

00:11:45.971 --> 00:11:51.076
who think "AR" stands
for "assault rifle."

00:11:51.076 --> 00:11:52.844
And we admitted that
we had made that mistake before,

00:11:52.844 --> 00:11:54.980
because it stands for Armalite,

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.716
which is the company
that originally made the gun.

00:11:57.716 --> 00:12:00.586
So, we -- I corrected myself
of making that error.

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:02.855
And then it got picked up
in some conservative press

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:08.160
who acted like I had
gotten caught by her.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.695
And reading it, I --

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:12.397
I started to think
for the first time,

00:12:12.397 --> 00:12:14.900
they might not be engaging
with the work.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.702
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.038 --> 00:12:20.372
So, I do really want
to stress again,

00:12:20.372 --> 00:12:25.044
I'm so sorry that
I got that wrong.

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:28.113
'Cause once you get the name
wrong, then you can't --

00:12:28.113 --> 00:12:29.815
can't talk about
anything else.

00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:33.886
'Cause that's not really --
my problem's not the name.

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:34.953
It's like the...

00:12:34.953 --> 00:12:36.288
It would be like
if someone was like,

00:12:36.288 --> 00:12:38.657
"Earth's gonna get hit
by an asteroid!"

00:12:38.657 --> 00:12:40.325
It's like,
"Um, it's not an asteroid

00:12:40.325 --> 00:12:42.595
once it enters the atmosphere."

00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:44.096
[ Laughter ]

00:12:44.096 --> 00:12:46.699
Still worried
about the asteroid.

00:12:46.699 --> 00:12:52.337
But I would like to continue
this conversation

00:12:52.337 --> 00:12:53.839
with the congresswoman,

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:56.175
so do please
stop by the studio anytime.

00:12:56.175 --> 00:12:59.711
We're located at
1250 Ditmars Boulevard,

00:12:59.711 --> 00:13:01.413
Queens, New York.

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:03.115
[ Laughter ]

00:13:07.185 --> 00:13:08.520
I got a...

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:11.323
A couple weeks ago,

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:14.426
we did a shot of whiskey
in "A Closer Look."

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:18.263
And afterwards, I received

00:13:18.263 --> 00:13:24.470
a bottle of
Wild Turkey Longbranch

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.305
from our friend
Matthew McConaughey.

00:13:26.305 --> 00:13:28.373
This is like two weeks ago,
and he wrote a note that said,

00:13:28.373 --> 00:13:30.408
"Saw you take a shot of whiskey
on air the other night.

00:13:30.408 --> 00:13:32.177
Thought you might need
a few more.

00:13:32.177 --> 00:13:34.346
Cheers, best, McConaughey."

00:13:34.346 --> 00:13:36.048
And he sent this bottle,

00:13:36.048 --> 00:13:39.351
and I thought it was
a pretty classy thing to do.

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:41.520
I mean, obviously,
part of it probably was

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.189
you know, he saw what we've been
doing for Pizza Hut.

00:13:44.189 --> 00:13:46.592
[ Laughter ]

00:13:52.231 --> 00:13:54.967
But, you know,
to have a sincere moment,

00:13:54.967 --> 00:13:56.568
it was very nice
'cause, you know, we did a shot

00:13:56.568 --> 00:13:58.070
because sometimes you get
overwhelmed by the news

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.738
and you do a shot.

00:13:59.738 --> 00:14:01.073
And that was very sweet of him.

00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:04.242
But I would like
to use this instead

00:14:04.242 --> 00:14:06.978
to toast Mr. McConaughey,

00:14:06.978 --> 00:14:09.014
because in the time
since he sent that,

00:14:09.014 --> 00:14:12.284
some terrible things
have happened, and he went out

00:14:12.284 --> 00:14:14.486
and he was a good man
who did a very hard thing

00:14:14.486 --> 00:14:16.321
with his comments the other day
at the White House.

00:14:16.321 --> 00:14:19.825
So, a toast
to Matthew McConaughey

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:22.260
and all the jackals out there.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.095
Let's try to stay optimistic,

00:14:24.095 --> 00:14:29.535
and you will all see me
next week,

00:14:29.535 --> 00:14:31.003
which I think...

00:14:31.003 --> 00:14:34.439
I think we're coming up on
like our 50th episode,

00:14:34.439 --> 00:14:36.274
which is a big deal.

00:14:36.274 --> 00:14:38.244
So, see you then.

